{
  "name": "Keratech 22 coarse 4.7 h FFT",
  "description": "Scaled-down Keratech 22 with the scope's own FFT stored per sweep (Kim, 2026-10-27). 7 temperatures 40-100 C in 10 C steps, 40 min each (the heater climbs 10 C in ~20 min at ~30 C/h, so the last two staircases of every level sit at a settled temperature). Within each level, four 10 min staircases 0-600-1200-1800-2400-3000-2400-1800-1200-600 rpm, 1 min per step; the 0 rpm minute is a stationary-bearing reference. Then 1 min at rest with SV 25. Scope: FFT ON with Kim's settings (AE/CHAN2, Hann, centre 107 kHz, span 500 kHz) - with it on every channel is 62,500 points, so timebase 0.1 s (FFT 0-312 kHz, channels 625 kS/s). UL volt_range 0.4: the UL750 output is ~80x lower since the 2026-10-27 move (0.019 V rms at 2963 rpm); re-size if it comes back. AE 5.0 (it reached 4 Vpp on 2026-10-20). PREREQUISITES: drive parameter 02-03 on communication and the pot at its bottom stop (on 2026-10-27 the drive held 50 Hz whatever was commanded); bearing lubricated; heater switched on by hand if started from the command line.",
